course: dictionary
lesson: 2178
title: A word from old armour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to long ago. Knights and soldiers used them, and today we rarely see them. «Corselet» is one of these words. When you meet it, use the words around it to work out what it means.
explain: The castle story gives you clues: «men-at-arms in casquet and corselet of steel» (helmets and armour). Men-at-arms are soldiers, and steel is a hard metal. So a corselet must be a piece of metal armour worn by a soldier.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you say «men-at-arms in helmet and armour of steel», the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
fact: A corselet was a piece of armour that covered the body, chest and back.
fact: In history, a corselet of steel or leather protected a soldier's chest.
fact: «Men-at-arms» means soldiers who fought in armour.
fact: «Portcullis» means a heavy gate that drops down to block a castle entrance.
fact: Today a corselet can also mean a tight piece of women's underwear, and in science it means the hard chest part (thorax) of an insect.
exercise: «men-at-arms in casquet and corselet of steel» (helmets and armour). What was a corselet in this sentence? | A dog that guards a castle | A gate that drops down over the entrance | A bird that sings at dawn | *A piece of steel armour for the body
exercise: In the castle story, what does «casquet» mean? | A small bell | A heavy gate | A horse's saddle | *A helmet
exercise: A beetle's corselet is its hard chest part. What is the corselet of an insect? | The soft part under its body | *The hard chest part, called the thorax | A pair of wings | The sharp feelers on its head
test: The knight wore a leather corselet that covered his chest and back. Which body parts did the corselet protect? | His legs and feet | His arms and hands | *His chest and back | His head and neck
test: In «the spiky portcullis» (a heavy gate that drops down), what is a portcullis? | A soldier's sword | *A heavy gate that drops down | A spiky plant in the garden | A kind of bridge over water
exam: The word «corselet» is rare today, and you find it in an old story. What should you do first? | Stop reading the story for the rest of the day | *Read the words around it for clues, then check with a dictionary | Guess it means a flower because it sounds pretty | Skip the whole sentence and never return to it
